  "result": "`docs/design/event-bus.md` (specifically its DES-052 section) is the document that specifies the actual mechanism: `emit()` maps every subscriber call, collects them via `Promise.allSettled`, and reports rejected results to `reportHandlerError()` without ever rethrowing from `emit()` itself — this is what makes handler isolation (and REQ-228's \"activity capture must not fail the originating write\") true structurally.\n\nOther docs — `docs/adr/ADR-022-activity-from-event-bus.md`, `docs/design/service-activity-and-attachment.md`, and `docs/design/repository-notification-and-activity.md` — all *invoke* this guarantee when explaining their own subscribers, but they attribute it back to the event bus's design rather than specifying the mechanism themselves. `docs/adr/ADR-005-in-process-event-bus.md` also documents the decision and its consequence at a higher level (\"one throwing handler never fails the emit or the sibling handlers\") but defers the actual mechanics to `event-bus.ts`/`event-bus.md`.\n\nANSWER: docs/design/event-bus.md",
